WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:02.135
[Joe] From portion sizes to exclusives,

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:05.005
we wanted to find out all
the differences between KFC

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:08.141
in the US, UK, Japan, and India.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.310
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.782
So, at the KFC in Japan, you
can order your chicken pieces

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:20.787
in, one piece, two pieces,
three pieces, four pieces

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:24.324
Five piece bucket that
comes with only leg pieces.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:27.093
In the UK you can get
buckets in three sizes,

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.194
you can get a six-piece.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.295
Eight pieces.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:33.333
And the largest one of them
all a 10-piece leg bucket.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.968
12 pieces.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.703
Or you can get a 14 piece.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.538
Or 16 piece bucket.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.473
Woo, that's a lot of chicken.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.345
In Japan, we have three drink sizes.

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.713
So we have a small.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.815
In the US our drinks come in medium.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.786
And this is what a large drink looks like.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:55.422
Here in India, we don't serve
cups, we just serve cans.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:02.429
If you want, you can also
get half a gallon bag

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.864
of your favorite drink of choice.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.466
Look at this thing.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.274
It's convenient.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:17.744
So the fries are the KFC in
Japan come in three sizes.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.412
So this is small.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.346
These are regular fries.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:24.918
And back again the large.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:28.121
Then we've got a box.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:33.760
Let us now measure the large
to see how much we get.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.095
You can do it.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:40.400
Now, of course the US
has a chicken sandwich.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.036
You can also get it spicy or classic.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:43.870
This is classic.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.106
I got this little guy, a Chicken Little,

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.507
look at this guy, huh?

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.341
There's the little guy.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.376
Comes of pickles, mayo.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.012
So instead of a chicken
sandwich, what we call ours

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.881
is the Chicken Fillet Burger.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.616
I think it's pretty much the same thing.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.451
It's like breaded and fried chicken

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:01.054
between two buns with some
lettuce and some mayonnaise.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:03.423
We also have something
called the Zinger Burger

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.258
which is pretty much the same thing,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.393
but the spice level is
amped up a little bit.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.330
You can also turn these
burgers into a Tower Burger.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.433
What that does is adds
cheese and a hash brown

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.602
to the burger, which in my opinion,

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.703
very worthwhile addition.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:20.440
Now we have special sandwiches.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.209
This one right here is
called Japanese-Style

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.644
Chicken Katsu Sandwich.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.513
So let's take a look inside.

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:29.315
So it's got mayo and it's got cabbage

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.784
and chicken katsu right there.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:34.821
(speaks in Japanese)

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:39.826
Hmm, oh, this sauce is
like soy sauce-based sauce

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.261
and it's a little bit sweet,

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:44.063
and this mayo is also
great with this sauce.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:49.068
This looks really small, but
it has huge amount of chicken.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.371
So if you eat this,
you're going to be full.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:56.376
And next one, we've got Chicken Fillet.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.078
Wow, this is also huge.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.014
Alright, so this one right here

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:04.117
is called Black Hot Sandwich.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.486
oh, look at this.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.421
It's like pepper mayo.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.657
I just tasted this pepper mayo

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:13.660
but it has a little like spiciness.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.231
Oh, man, it's too strong.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.500
I wouldn't get it, be careful.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.302
All right, let's move on
to chicken sandwiches.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.704
Here in India, we don't have
an American Chicken Sandwich

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:26.539
but we have a Zinger

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:30.109
and a smaller sandwich
called a Krisper, cute.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.811
The Krisper looks like it wants to grow up

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.246
and be a Zinger someday.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:36.015
They also come in two
variants: Spicy Krisper

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.084
and a Tandoori Zinger.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.285
Let's taste all of them.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.122
Oh, that's pretty yummy.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.958
They've used a different
kind of mayonnaise here.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:49.229
It has a bit of sweetness to
it and a spicy kick at the end.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:53.066
And now for the legendary
Zinger, back in the day

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.535
there were only two fast
food chains here in India.

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.103
It was McDonald's and KFC.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:04:00.273
And while McDonald's had more
affordable burger options

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:03.676
the KFC Zinger was so delicious,

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.878
it was always a treat to eat.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.717
Mmh, and it still is.

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:13.753
I love that they use
a whole boneless piece

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.655
of proper chicken in there.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:18.258
Delicious mayo, it's so delicious.

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:20.226
Okay, now let's try the spicy variants.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:22.795
This is the Spicy Krisper.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.330
Look at this sauce.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.432
It's almost blood-red.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.267
I'm excited.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:34.507
Oh my God, the sauce almost
has a szechuan taste to it.

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:37.644
Next up, the Zinger, but tandoori.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:43.249
Hmm, I love the fullness of the chicken

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.985
that comes in these burgers versus

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.655
like a mince chicken patty
in other restaurants.

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:51.557
And so much bite to it, so juicy tender.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:52.859
That all sounds amazing.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.661
Stop, you're going too fast.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:56.863
I have to say, those
sandwiches look delicious

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:59.065
and I am jealous.

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.100
All right, moving away from chicken,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.203
India's KFC actually has
vegetarian alternatives

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.705
for all our burgers.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:10.043
That is a Vegetarian Krisper,
a Vegetarian Spicy Krisper

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:12.412
and a Vegetarian Zinger.

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:15.782
Now while India has a majority
population of non-vegetarians

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:19.118
around 70 percent, there is
a huge vegetarian population,

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.820
which is why a lot of
fast food restaurants

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.289
have to make sure they have
a lot of vegetarian options

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.525
on their menu to make it more approachable

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.994
and acceptable for all people over here.

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:30.863
There's also levels to
vegetarianism over here

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.599
that are, "I will eat egg
but not chicken" vegetarians.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:36.469
There are, "I will eat fish
but not lamb" vegetarians.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.171
There are, "I will eat the curry

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.939
but not the pieces" vegetarians.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:43.042
There are, "I am vegetarian
only on Tuesdays" vegetarians.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.677
There are, "I have made a promise to God

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.546
for this one month" vegetarians.

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:48.047
There are, "I am vegetarians,

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:50.783
so you will all be
vegetarian" vegetarians.

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:53.953
They're the weird ones and we
try not to talk about them,

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:58.658
which is why KFC in India
brands itself as just KFC.

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:01.227
There's no Kentucky Fried
Chicken anywhere here

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:03.730
because obviously I'm not
going to go to a place

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.765
that's named that if I'm one of these

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:07.567
many types of vegetarians.

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:12.572
KFC in America has extra-crispy chicken.

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:13.840
This is the best type of chicken.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:14.707
I mean, look at this.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:15.975
I don't know what they do to this

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:18.211
but the skin is practically falling off.

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.580
It is so crispy and so delicious.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.382
I love extra crispy so much.

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:25.585
So we also have Dip Pack, oh.

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:30.590
So it's got Colonel
Crispy and some nuggets

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:36.896
and boneless Kentucky and
some original chicken.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:39.766
So this Dip Pack, it
comes with these fries.

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:42.602
So if you want to have a little bigger one

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.737
you can order Dip Barrel.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:47.340
I mean it's double amount of this Dip Pack

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.775
so it's going to be very big.

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:50.276
So this one right here,

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:53.379
is called Four-piece Red Hot Chicken Box

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:56.349
and it comes with a pie and fry

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:59.619
and a medium drink.

00:06:59.619 --> 00:07:02.789
And actually we have other box options,

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:06.492
like Four-piece Half Hot
and Half Original Box,

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:08.795
And it comes with fries as well

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:13.132
and Six-piece Half Hot
and Half Original Box,

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:14.734
it comes with fries again.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:19.305
So in Japan we have (speaks Japanese).

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:24.243
That means Chicken Day, it's
on every 28th of the month.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:29.248
And two stands for "ni"
and eight stands for "wa"

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:31.651
and it becomes "niwa."

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:35.054
And niwa is synonymous with niwatori.

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:37.356
Niwatori means "chicken."

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.992
So that's what it's called, "Chicken Day."

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.828
Okay, let's start with chicken in India.

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:43.396
Apart from the crispy chicken,

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:47.133
we also get Smoky Red Chicken.

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:49.769
Oof, wow.

00:07:49.769 --> 00:07:53.072
I believe this is KFC's
answer to tandoori chicken.

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:54.440
If you guys don't know what a tandoori is,

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.342
it's basically a cylindrical oven

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:59.645
that they light up using
word fire or charcoal.

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:02.281
And it adds a really smoky flavor

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:04.650
to the meats or breads
that you cook inside of it.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:08.154
I doubt KFC's across the
country have an actual tandoor

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.923
but the flavoring
definitely smells of that.

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:12.959
The marinade looks like that.

00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:17.697
Oh my God!

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:19.532
That's actually pretty good.

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:20.633
You know what, KFC?

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:22.869
Pretty good job.

00:08:22.869 --> 00:08:24.504
You have to remember, KFC is competing

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:28.341
with a lot of Mughlai restaurants
across every Indian city.

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:31.277
And while this doesn't have
as much of that smoky char

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:34.881
that a lot of tandoori kebabs
have, it has a lot of flavor,

00:08:34.881 --> 00:08:37.316
and the chicken is quite juicy.

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:38.484
Good job.

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:41.454
It's super spicy though,
so if you're somebody

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:44.690
who can't handle spice, go
a little easier on this one.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:47.660
When an Indian says
something's spicy, it's spicy.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.095
The pot pie that they have here,

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:51.697
they're not kidding when
they say pie and the pot pie.

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:53.332
How thick this is.

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:55.234
I gotta say the pot pie
actually looks quite good.

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:57.270
We love meat pies here in the UK,

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:58.971
you'll often see people
tucking into like a steak

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:01.007
and kidney pie or a chicken pie,

00:09:01.007 --> 00:09:02.575
but yeah, they should probably put that

00:09:02.575 --> 00:09:03.409
on the menu over here.

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:04.777
I think they'd cash in
on the British market.

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:07.947
Speaking of big dishes of
stuff, the Famous Bowl.

00:09:07.947 --> 00:09:11.250
Once upon a time, a KFC employee was like,

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:13.486
"I could have put everything into one dish

00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:14.654
and call it a day."

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:16.722
And ta-da, the Famous Bowl was born.

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:18.858
This has to be like three pounds

00:09:18.858 --> 00:09:20.192
Now, Joe, I'm glad you also think

00:09:20.192 --> 00:09:21.661
that the Famous Bowl doesn't do that great

00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:23.262
because, to me, that
looks like a nightmare.

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:27.333
We currently have a Nashville
Hot Chicken and Hot Tenders.

00:09:27.333 --> 00:09:28.501
I went ahead with the tenders.

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:30.403
I've just been informed
this was a big TikTok thing

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:32.305
for a minute, something about
biting it and crunching it.

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:33.372
I don't know anything about that,

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:34.740
I can say just by holding this

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.342
there's no way these are crispy.

00:09:38.511 --> 00:09:41.080
Well, it's not that spicy, it's not spicy.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.815
I do like this a lot.

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:47.019
I'm going to stop eating up.

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:49.388
Oh, that heat's catching up with me.

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:51.023
Slow burn, slow build on the heat.

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:55.428
All right, so here we've
got two Special Twisters.

00:09:55.428 --> 00:09:59.865
So this one right here is called
Pepper Mayonnaise Twister.

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:02.501
Oh, it looks great.

00:10:07.807 --> 00:10:09.809
Nine out of 10.

00:10:09.809 --> 00:10:11.477
KFC, thank you.

00:10:11.477 --> 00:10:13.479
Thank you for making me happy.

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:18.484
So next we got, oh, Teriyaki
Twister, should be great.

00:10:19.352 --> 00:10:20.753
It's kinda gross.

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:25.891
It's got mayo and Colonel
Crispy, some veggies,

00:10:25.891 --> 00:10:28.761
and I hope this is teriyaki sauce.

00:10:29.629 --> 00:10:31.263
(speaks in Japanese)

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:38.037
Mmh, mmh, mmh.

00:10:38.037 --> 00:10:42.408
It looks gross, but it tastes incredible.

00:10:42.408 --> 00:10:45.144
10 out of 10, congratulations.

00:10:46.278 --> 00:10:48.981
Oishi, it means delicious.

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:50.650
Look how tiny those twisters are.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.285
I can eat like three of
those easily, easily.

00:10:53.285 --> 00:10:57.156
I said this one right here,
it's called Colonel Crispy,

00:10:57.156 --> 00:10:58.457
is it only in Japan?

00:10:58.457 --> 00:11:01.394
I cannot confirm the difference
between a Colonel Crispy

00:11:01.394 --> 00:11:03.162
and a KFC chicken tender.

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:05.164
They call their tenders Colonel Crispies.

00:11:05.164 --> 00:11:08.834
And we call our Colonel
Crispies, chicken tenders.

00:11:08.834 --> 00:11:10.202
There's a few other, the
language differences,

00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:11.504
like instead of chicken tenders,

00:11:11.504 --> 00:11:13.673
we call ours chicken mini-fillets.

00:11:13.673 --> 00:11:16.308
It's been a while since I ordered this one

00:11:16.308 --> 00:11:19.045
but it still has crispy bits.

00:11:20.546 --> 00:11:21.380
Good job.

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:25.851
Japanese KFC's technology,
state of the art.

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:27.653
One iconic dish that you'll find

00:11:27.653 --> 00:11:30.823
on the KFC India menu is biryani.

00:11:30.823 --> 00:11:34.293
And so KFC India has
taken a very bold decision

00:11:34.293 --> 00:11:36.128
to launch their own biryanis.

00:11:36.128 --> 00:11:37.763
They come in four flavors.

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:40.700
Number one: Classic
Chicken, nice and crispy.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.235
Number two: Popcorn Chicken.

00:11:43.235 --> 00:11:47.440
number three: the Spicy Red
Chicken that I really enjoy.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.341
And number four: the Veg Patty,

00:11:49.341 --> 00:11:53.312
which it's so tempting to
just push that to the side

00:11:53.312 --> 00:11:57.183
because veg biryani is
already just a concept

00:11:57.183 --> 00:11:59.051
but really not a fan of over here.

00:12:00.252 --> 00:12:04.590
But just for now, you can stay here.

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:08.127
Okay, I'm going to begin with
the Popcorn Chicken Biryani,

00:12:08.127 --> 00:12:11.764
which is just so
blasphemous to begin with.

00:12:20.372 --> 00:12:25.344
It's not a biryani, it's,
I'm so upset right now.

00:12:26.011 --> 00:12:28.914
This one, the Spicy Red Chicken,

00:12:28.914 --> 00:12:31.183
has a bit of that tandoori wipe to it.

00:12:31.183 --> 00:12:33.853
They really tried to
overcompensate with the spices,

00:12:33.853 --> 00:12:35.988
there's a lot of clove flavor.

00:12:35.988 --> 00:12:37.456
Just to convince you,
you are eating a biryani,

00:12:37.456 --> 00:12:40.025
so go easy on that curry.

00:12:42.361 --> 00:12:44.663
I could eat this, like if I was hungry,

00:12:44.663 --> 00:12:45.898
not a biryani though.

00:12:45.898 --> 00:12:49.034
Also the US KFC that you
can't get in Japan are wings.

00:12:49.034 --> 00:12:53.372
You can get wings at the
KFC in units of six, 12,

00:12:53.372 --> 00:12:54.874
24 or 48.

00:12:54.874 --> 00:12:56.742
I believe the three wing flavors

00:12:56.742 --> 00:13:01.447
that I got here are standard
Buffalo, the Honey Barbecue,

00:13:01.447 --> 00:13:04.383
and if you're at total wuss, unsauced?

00:13:04.383 --> 00:13:05.918
What's wrong with you?

00:13:05.918 --> 00:13:07.253
Yeah, very sketchy.

00:13:07.253 --> 00:13:11.857
You can also get them in a
limited time Nashville Hot Sauce.

00:13:11.857 --> 00:13:14.193
All right, so we have nuggets.

00:13:14.193 --> 00:13:18.397
We have three pieces, five pieces,

00:13:18.397 --> 00:13:21.734
and they come with only ketchup.

00:13:21.734 --> 00:13:22.868
Our biscuit on the other hand

00:13:22.868 --> 00:13:26.071
is just this Southern
style, not exactly a scone

00:13:26.071 --> 00:13:27.740
but kind of looks like
one from a distance.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.509
Dry cornmeal biscuit.

00:13:30.509 --> 00:13:34.380
Oh yeah.

00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:40.286
Here we've got KFC biscuit.

00:13:40.286 --> 00:13:44.056
It comes with Honey Maple KFC.

00:13:44.056 --> 00:13:45.658
Ah.

00:13:51.063 --> 00:13:54.767
This is good, but maple, it's
a little bit sweet for me.

00:13:54.767 --> 00:13:55.768
Mac and cheese,

00:13:55.768 --> 00:13:58.270
I can't believe you guys do
not have macaroni and cheese.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.905
Love mac and cheese.

00:13:59.905 --> 00:14:01.273
Mashed potatoes and gravy.

00:14:01.273 --> 00:14:02.374
You don't have that in Japan?

00:14:02.374 --> 00:14:06.979
Guys, guys, demand this
from your Japanese KFC,

00:14:06.979 --> 00:14:08.547
you want the mashed potatoes and gravy.

00:14:08.547 --> 00:14:09.849
Now we have a slightly different approach

00:14:09.849 --> 00:14:12.351
to sides in the UK compared to the US.

00:14:12.351 --> 00:14:15.387
For example, our corn comes on the cob.

00:14:15.387 --> 00:14:17.289
Baked beans, these are slightly different

00:14:17.289 --> 00:14:20.092
to the regular beans that you
might put on toast in the UK.

00:14:20.092 --> 00:14:22.795
They have kind of a barbecue
sauce flavor to them.

00:14:22.795 --> 00:14:25.464
And now for the quickest sauce talk ever.

00:14:25.464 --> 00:14:26.398
[Announcer] "Sauce talk."

00:14:26.398 --> 00:14:27.399
KFC Sauce.

00:14:30.035 --> 00:14:33.272
The KFC Sauce is like
a brown mustard mayo.

00:14:33.272 --> 00:14:34.874
Yeah, the sauce is good.

00:14:34.874 --> 00:14:37.509
There are a few sources which
are exclusive to the UK.

00:14:37.509 --> 00:14:41.013
For example, we have this
Spicy Supercharger Dip,

00:14:41.013 --> 00:14:43.883
which is kind of like a
spicy mayo type thing.

00:14:43.883 --> 00:14:47.052
We have some sweet chili
sauce, garlic mayonnaise,

00:14:47.052 --> 00:14:48.721
another really good option.

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:50.623
Garlic mayo on chips.

00:14:50.623 --> 00:14:51.724
It's just fantastic.

00:14:51.724 --> 00:14:55.127
These three dipping sauces.

00:14:55.127 --> 00:15:00.132
So, we've got barbecue sauce and mustard.

00:15:00.232 --> 00:15:03.936
And this pink one is called Mentaiko Mayo.

00:15:03.936 --> 00:15:06.772
mentaiko means is like spicy cod roe

00:15:06.772 --> 00:15:09.541
and a very popular taste in Japan.

00:15:09.541 --> 00:15:10.643
This is actually great.

00:15:10.643 --> 00:15:12.211
I'll dip this.

00:15:12.211 --> 00:15:13.312
Mmh.

00:15:15.848 --> 00:15:18.450
It tastes fantastic.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:19.285
Winner.

00:15:20.419 --> 00:15:22.688
India does not have too
many exclusive dips.

00:15:22.688 --> 00:15:25.124
In fact, we just have a
veg eggless mayonnaise

00:15:25.124 --> 00:15:27.559
and a tandoori masala mayonnaise.

00:15:27.559 --> 00:15:28.861
It's time to taste.

00:15:30.296 --> 00:15:32.264
I'm using the same hand
because here in India

00:15:32.264 --> 00:15:34.166
we don't eat with our left hand.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:38.971
If you're wondering why,
commenters, you let them know.

00:15:40.506 --> 00:15:44.843
Why don't Indians eat
with their left hand?

00:15:53.352 --> 00:15:55.220
Well, it's just mayonnaise,

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.389
so good job on that.

00:15:59.491 --> 00:16:02.695
Mayonnaise again with a
little bit of a sweet,

00:16:02.695 --> 00:16:04.897
but also spicy kick to it.

00:16:04.897 --> 00:16:07.533
I wish we had more options,
especially considering

00:16:07.533 --> 00:16:11.603
there are so many different
delicious chicken options.

00:16:11.603 --> 00:16:15.240
I love to be able to dip
my tenders in more sauces.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.343
That is a weird sentence.

00:16:17.343 --> 00:16:18.644
Desserts at a US KFC.

00:16:18.644 --> 00:16:20.612
You can get this chocolate chip cookie.

00:16:20.612 --> 00:16:22.047
Recognize that guy?

00:16:22.047 --> 00:16:24.450
(chuckles) I just look just like this guy.

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:28.420
And finally, a chocolate chip cake.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.956
Here in India, we have
two exclusive desserts

00:16:30.956 --> 00:16:35.761
a choco mud pie and a coffee mousse cake.

00:16:35.761 --> 00:16:37.796
Oh boy!

00:16:37.796 --> 00:16:40.466
Just look at this cross
section, my friend.

00:16:40.466 --> 00:16:43.635
Next up, coffee mousse cake.

00:16:45.637 --> 00:16:50.642
Yeah, these are pretty
average as desserts.

00:16:51.076 --> 00:16:52.044
Fountain drinks.

00:16:52.044 --> 00:16:52.878
There's a few that we can get

00:16:52.878 --> 00:16:55.547
that you guys cannot over there in Japan.

00:16:55.547 --> 00:16:57.816
The first one is a beverage

00:16:57.816 --> 00:17:02.121
that I have yet to make one
human being who enjoys it.

00:17:02.121 --> 00:17:03.822
Of course, I'm talking about Sierra Mist

00:17:03.822 --> 00:17:05.624
maybe grossest soda ever.

00:17:07.826 --> 00:17:09.128
It's so bad.

00:17:09.128 --> 00:17:11.063
Another drink that you can get at KFC

00:17:11.063 --> 00:17:12.664
that you can't get at Japan.

00:17:12.664 --> 00:17:13.866
And here it is right here.

00:17:13.866 --> 00:17:15.534
Mountains Dew is great.

00:17:15.534 --> 00:17:16.702
When I was in college, I
worked at a pizza place.

00:17:16.702 --> 00:17:18.604
I drank so much Mountain Dew I threw up

00:17:18.604 --> 00:17:19.872
and now I'm drinking Mountain Dew,

00:17:19.872 --> 00:17:20.706
let's see if I can do it again.

00:17:20.706 --> 00:17:24.076
My favorite beverage,
Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning.

00:17:25.544 --> 00:17:26.879
So good, so good.

00:17:26.879 --> 00:17:30.049
So here we've got
Japanese exclusive drinks.

00:17:30.049 --> 00:17:33.519
This one right here is water,

00:17:34.887 --> 00:17:38.957
but it comes with this Assam tea pack.

00:17:40.059 --> 00:17:43.095
It's supposed to be hot, but it's cold.

00:17:43.095 --> 00:17:46.065
And next one, we've got coffee.

00:17:46.065 --> 00:17:50.069
And this one right here
is roasted rich coffee.

00:17:50.069 --> 00:17:53.372
(speaks in Japanese)

00:17:53.372 --> 00:17:56.909
It's a little bit bitter
than that normal coffee.

00:17:56.909 --> 00:18:00.846
And here we got all Earl Grey iced tea.

00:18:00.846 --> 00:18:02.014
It's not sweet at all.

00:18:02.014 --> 00:18:05.017
And next one, it melon soda.

00:18:05.017 --> 00:18:07.319
It has bright green color.

00:18:12.024 --> 00:18:12.858
Horrible.

00:18:12.858 --> 00:18:13.792
It's too sweet.

00:18:13.792 --> 00:18:17.229
Here is ginger ale, nothing special.

00:18:17.229 --> 00:18:21.033
And the last one, it's not
Natchan Refreshing Orange.

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:26.038
Exclusive drinks in KFC,
India, we have Mirinda,

00:18:26.338 --> 00:18:29.007
which is an orange soda and Red Bull.

00:18:29.007 --> 00:18:31.076
Let's talk about Mirinda.

00:18:31.076 --> 00:18:34.113
This is a drink that
really evokes nostalgia.

00:18:34.113 --> 00:18:37.182
Nineties kids really know
what I'm talking about

00:18:37.182 --> 00:18:38.016
when I say:

00:18:40.352 --> 00:18:42.554
Mirinda.

00:18:42.554 --> 00:18:45.858
The drinks are just
normal, nothing special

00:18:45.858 --> 00:18:50.129
but chickens are finger-licking good.

00:18:51.063 --> 00:18:53.465
Now, usually we'd have even
more exclusive menu items

00:18:53.465 --> 00:18:55.634
to show you, but unfortunately UK KFCs

00:18:55.634 --> 00:18:57.903
are currently operating
with a reduced menu.

00:18:57.903 --> 00:19:02.908
Here's what you could normally
find on the menu at a UK KFC.

00:19:04.843 --> 00:19:08.147
A vegan burger, the Big Daddy Burger,

00:19:08.147 --> 00:19:10.449
a range of chicken wraps

00:19:10.449 --> 00:19:15.454
some rice boxes, onion
rings, curry sauce, Krushems

00:19:16.488 --> 00:19:18.257
and a full range of hot drinks

00:19:18.257 --> 00:19:21.660
including English Breakfast tea.

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:24.062
So let's talk about Christmas in Japan.

00:19:24.062 --> 00:19:27.766
So Christmas is one of the
biggest events in Japan

00:19:27.766 --> 00:19:29.768
even though about one percent

00:19:29.768 --> 00:19:32.070
of Japanese people are Christians,

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:35.841
we just enter Christmas
as just a fun event.

00:19:35.841 --> 00:19:39.178
And as for KFC for Christmas in Japan

00:19:39.178 --> 00:19:44.183
back in 1970s, Japan KFC
launched a hugely successful

00:19:44.883 --> 00:19:48.854
advertising campaign called
(speaks in Japanese),

00:19:48.854 --> 00:19:51.356
that's "Kentucky for Christmas."

00:19:51.356 --> 00:19:54.426
And with that strong marketing campaign

00:19:54.426 --> 00:19:58.730
it became so popular to have
KFC for Christmas in Japan.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:03.535
And now about 3.6 million
Japanese families eat KFC

00:20:03.535 --> 00:20:04.503
for Christmas.

00:20:04.503 --> 00:20:07.439
And talking about my
personal experiences, yes,

00:20:07.439 --> 00:20:10.442
when I was young, I would
eat KFC for Christmas

00:20:10.442 --> 00:20:14.346
with my family but when you start dating,

00:20:14.346 --> 00:20:16.582
Christmas makes a transformation

00:20:16.582 --> 00:20:20.485
from a family event to couples event

00:20:20.485 --> 00:20:22.387
and I'm looking for the one

00:20:22.387 --> 00:20:25.123
who can enjoy KFC for Christmas with me.

00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:32.130
In the UK a drum is 170 calories.

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:36.768
So in Japan, one drum stick of - Oh.

00:20:36.768 --> 00:20:40.105
So in Japan, one drums
stick of Original Chicken

00:20:40.105 --> 00:20:43.709
on average has 237 calories.

00:20:43.709 --> 00:20:46.211
Chicken's looking a
little limp there George.

00:20:46.211 --> 00:20:49.348
In the US one stiff drumstick

00:20:49.348 --> 00:20:51.883
of Original Recipe is 130 calories,

00:20:51.883 --> 00:20:56.321
but according to KFC's US site,
that's for a 53 gram piece.

00:20:56.321 --> 00:20:59.992
Now, adjusting for the 87 gram
piece, like that of Japan,

00:20:59.992 --> 00:21:02.628
the calories go up to 210.

00:21:02.628 --> 00:21:03.462
Does that make sense?

00:21:03.462 --> 00:21:04.296
Great.

00:21:04.296 --> 00:21:06.632
Now, take this bad boy
and make him extra crispy,

00:21:06.632 --> 00:21:09.167
and you got 270 calories.

00:21:10.969 --> 00:21:13.171
It's too many calories.

00:21:13.171 --> 00:21:16.375
Mm, not enough calories if you ask me.

00:21:16.375 --> 00:21:19.211
But finger licking good.

00:21:19.211 --> 00:21:21.580
I think KFC got to George, he
keeps dropping that slogan.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:22.414
Are they paying George?

00:21:22.414 --> 00:21:24.983
I think George is getting some
money on the side from KFC.

00:21:24.983 --> 00:21:27.352
Oh my God, if George turns
out to be Colonel Sanders,

00:21:27.352 --> 00:21:28.754
I will lose my mind.

00:21:28.754 --> 00:21:30.822
We should also point out
that the KFC India website

00:21:30.822 --> 00:21:32.824
is a major need of an update.

00:21:32.824 --> 00:21:35.227
There is an FAQ page where
people have asked things

00:21:35.227 --> 00:21:37.729
like, "How many calories
does this chicken have?"

00:21:37.729 --> 00:21:41.433
Or, "Sometimes, I see red
deposits in my chicken.

00:21:41.433 --> 00:21:43.335
What is it?"

00:21:43.335 --> 00:21:45.003
And for almost all of these questions

00:21:45.003 --> 00:21:47.039
the answers are just filler text.

00:21:47.039 --> 00:21:49.341
So if you ask me what
those red deposits are,

00:21:49.341 --> 00:21:51.243
I genuinely don't know.

00:21:53.278 --> 00:21:54.813
Unfortunately, KFC in the UK

00:21:54.813 --> 00:21:56.281
doesn't disclose its ingredients.

00:21:56.281 --> 00:21:58.950
In the US our Original Recipe
Chicken ingredients are:

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:02.087
first with the fresh chicken,
it is marinated with salt,

00:22:02.087 --> 00:22:04.756
sodium phosphate, and
monosodium glutamate.

00:22:04.756 --> 00:22:07.326
Onto the breading, it's
breaded with salt, wheat flour,

00:22:07.326 --> 00:22:10.562
tricalcium phosphate,
maltodextrin, triglycerides,

00:22:10.562 --> 00:22:15.500
natural flavor, Colonel's Secret
Original Recipe seasoning.

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:18.870
So KFC in Japan doesn't
disclose their ingredients.

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:21.573
So we emailed their customer support

00:22:21.573 --> 00:22:24.076
and this is what they told us.

00:22:26.011 --> 00:22:28.080
Unfortunately, KFC does not share

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:30.215
a full list of ingredients
with the public.

00:22:30.215 --> 00:22:32.184
So what do we know about KFC?

00:22:32.184 --> 00:22:35.821
Well, the KFC India website
has a couple of clues.

00:22:35.821 --> 00:22:38.256
We know that all of our
chicken is farmed here

00:22:38.256 --> 00:22:39.224
and not imported.

00:22:39.224 --> 00:22:43.395
And all of it is 100 percent
whole muscle chicken.

00:22:44.496 --> 00:22:46.765
That means it's made from
whole pieces of chicken

00:22:46.765 --> 00:22:48.734
and not cut together mince chicken

00:22:48.734 --> 00:22:50.235
like you find in chicken nuggets.

00:22:50.235 --> 00:22:53.271
In fact, the website says they
have an Open Kitchen Policy.

00:22:53.271 --> 00:22:56.108
And what that means is
anybody can walk into a KFC

00:22:56.108 --> 00:22:58.343
and apparently ask for a kitchen tour

00:22:58.343 --> 00:23:01.279
and you can go into the kitchen,
look at everything and ask

00:23:01.279 --> 00:23:02.881
as many questions as you want.

00:23:02.881 --> 00:23:04.950
Indian chicken farmers
were previously criticized

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:06.918
for overusing antibiotics.

00:23:06.918 --> 00:23:08.387
As recently as 2018,

00:23:08.387 --> 00:23:10.489
the Bureau of Investigative
Journalism found out

00:23:10.489 --> 00:23:13.158
that a lot of Indian farmers
were feeding colistin

00:23:13.158 --> 00:23:15.127
to their chickens as a growth promoter

00:23:15.127 --> 00:23:16.995
without any medical supervision.

00:23:16.995 --> 00:23:19.197
Colistin is known as the antibiotic

00:23:19.197 --> 00:23:20.265
of the last resort.

00:23:20.265 --> 00:23:21.600
Holy sh--!

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:24.770
Oh my God, that's so frightening

00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:26.405
and is only given to humans

00:23:26.405 --> 00:23:28.640
when other antibiotics have failed.

00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:30.809
So if we give our chickens colistin

00:23:30.809 --> 00:23:33.779
then the humans who consume it
might become resistant to it.

00:23:33.779 --> 00:23:37.315
In fact, they can develop a
antibiotic resistant superbug

00:23:37.315 --> 00:23:38.450
and that's not good.

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:41.987
Yuelei, this sounds like
the plot to a horror movie.

00:23:41.987 --> 00:23:44.423
What is he talking about?

00:23:44.423 --> 00:23:46.091
That is terrifying.

00:23:46.091 --> 00:23:48.493
I'm going to assume we don't do that here,

00:23:48.493 --> 00:23:51.196
and if we do, oh God!

00:23:51.196 --> 00:23:53.432
But when the report came out
talking about the ill effects

00:23:53.432 --> 00:23:55.934
of colistin, India ended
up banning it completely,

00:23:55.934 --> 00:23:58.970
so we're safe from colistin at last.

00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:01.473
I kind of look like
Colonel Sanders, right?

00:24:01.473 --> 00:24:03.008
Look, this guy

00:24:03.008 --> 00:24:04.776
I'm a younger Colonel Sanders.

00:24:04.776 --> 00:24:05.911
KFC is doing any sort

00:24:05.911 --> 00:24:08.713
of the adventures of Young
Colonel Sanders ad campaign.

00:24:09.815 --> 00:24:11.750
Is this a face that could sell chicken?

